# Card section (title + description + card)

Use for stacked detail/settings blocks: a **tight** stack of **title** (`h2`) + optional **description** (`p`), then a clear gap, then controls inside the card body.

`SettingsFormSection` is a thin alias of **`CardSection`** (required `description`) for settings pages that mirror **Settings → Appearance**.

## Rules

- **Do not** put `h2`, description `p`, and `Card` as **direct siblings** under `space-y-2` — that adds extra gap between title and description (Tailwind spaces every child).
- **Do** wrap **title + description** (+ optional **note**) in a **single** header block so only **one** `space-y-2` step sits between that intro and the card.
- Prefer **`CardSection`** from `@engenty/ui-core` instead of hand-rolling the markup. Use **`SettingsFormSection`** only when you want the settings-oriented name with a required description.

## Component

- **`CardSection`** (`packages/ui-core/src/components/ui/card-section.tsx`) — figure: header outside, body on `SettingsFormCard`, optional caption below.
- **`SettingsFormCard`** — bordered surface; variants `default` | `compact` | `flush`.
- Convenience props: `title`, `description?`, `note?`, `titleAction?`, `headerVariant?`, `cardVariant?`, `cardClassName?`, `children`.
- Compound: `CardSection.Header`, `CardSection.Body`, `CardSection.Caption`.

### Header variants (`headerVariant` / `Header variant`)

| Variant | Use |
|---|---|
| `default` | Form/detail section title (`font-medium text-lg`) |
| `meta` | Overview / quiet labels (muted uppercase) |
| `display` | Hub / display sections (`font-heading`) |

Do **not** paste title Tailwind classes — pick a variant.
## Example

```tsx
import { CardSection } from "@engenty/ui-core";

// Convenience
<CardSection title={t("sections.general")} description={t("sections.generalDesc")}>
  {/* rows, selects, etc. */}
</CardSection>

// Compound (e.g. flush KV list / meta overview label)
<CardSection>
  <CardSection.Header title={t("sectionBilling")} />
  <CardSection.Body className="space-y-0 divide-y divide-border/50" variant="flush">
    {rows}
  </CardSection.Body>
</CardSection>

<CardSection.Header title={t("detail.company")} variant="meta" />
```

## Inside the body (no cascading cards)

`CardSection` already wraps convenience `children` in **`CardSection.Body`** / `SettingsFormCard`. Do **not** nest another **`Card`** inside children.

- **Tables:** render `<Table>` directly as children.
- **Subgroups:** dividers / flat tinted blocks — not a second card chrome.
- **`cardVariant="compact"`** + `cardClassName="space-y-0 divide-y divide-border"` for stacked `SettingsFormRow`s.

## When not to use

- List/catalog sections where the body is **not** a single form card — keep a local layout.
- Overview muted uppercase labels without a card (contacts Overview) — different primitive.
- Auth / dialog cards that use **`CardHeader` inside** the surface — keep on `Card`.
